00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:51.000
It tends to be a longer term trauma-based, trauma-informed treatment where there's three stages, roughly speaking. When the client first comes in, they tend to be struggling with profound depression, like I mentioned, but also many of these folks have a lot of self-harm, like cutting or burning, and they often are in research terms. The research is clear they are some of the most suicidal clients in the mental health field. So there needs to be a lot of stabilization. So they need some help, for example.
这往往是一种长期的、基于创伤的、创伤知情的治疗，大致分为三个阶段。当客户刚来时，他们往往像我提到的那样，正处于严重的抑郁中，而且这些人中许多人有严重的自残行为，比如割伤或烧伤，在研究术语中，研究很清楚，他们是心理健康领域自杀倾向最高的客户之一。因此，需要大量的稳定化工作。所以他们需要一些帮助，例如。

